		"_postman_id": "3f7a91c4-2d6b-4e18-a5c3-8b7d0e4f2a91",
		"name": "Points Of Interest",
		"description": "Every operation the service publishes, in the order the collection runner needs them.\n\nThe folders mirror the documentation pages: `Use cases` renders `docs/USE_CASES.md`, `Queries` renders `docs/QUERIES.md`, and `Health` renders `docs/HEALTH.md`. Each request keeps the name of its `operationId` summary in `openapi.yaml`, so a request and its contract are found under the same words.\n\nRunning the whole collection top to bottom works on a fresh stack, and it works again on the same stack. `Register a point of interest` builds a name that is unique per run, so the uniqueness constraint never turns a rerun into a conflict, and it stores the identifier it gets back.\n\n`baseUrl` is a collection variable, so the collection runs with no environment imported. Import `points-of-interest-local.postman_environment.json` to point it somewhere else.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
